sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User
  participant GLFW
  participant WM as WindowManager
  participant HTML as HTMLRendererMT
  participant RUI as ReactiveUI
  participant UIState as game.lua methods
  participant Game as GameLogic.lua
  participant State as LuaUIState

  User->>GLFW: press START GAME
  GLFW->>WM: click_callback(window x/y)
  WM->>HTML: C++ input handler (LIFO)
  HTML->>HTML: window→framebuffer coordinates
  HTML->>HTML: reverse hit-test rendered bounds
  HTML->>RUI: DispatchEvent("click", "onStartGame", event)
  RUI->>UIState: methods.onStartGame(state)
  UIState->>Game: start("standard")
  Game->>State: SetUIValue(...), including gameStarted=true
  Game->>RUI: RefreshUI()
  RUI-->>HTML: newly evaluated HTML (startup screen removed)
  HTML-->>WM: true / consumed

  alt no C++ handler consumes click
    WM->>WM: append click to Lua EventQueue
    Note over WM,HTML: GameInput.lua later calls HandleClickEvent as a fallback path.
  end
